# Mermaid Formatting

- When adding Mermaid diagrams to notes or guides, use `<br>` for line breaks inside node labels.
- Do not use escaped newline sequences like `\n` in Mermaid node labels.
- For Typora compatibility, avoid Mermaid reserved words such as `loop` as participant or node aliases.
- In sequence diagrams, quote participant display names when they contain spaces or punctuation, for example `participant UI as "ChatWidget / BottomPane"`.
- Avoid `->` inside sequence message text; write `to` or another plain-word description instead.
- Keep diagrams compact and supportive of the surrounding explanation.
